{
  "order": 13000,
  "name": "Drill-down checks",
  "kind": "function",
  "responsibility": "What a board can say about a link to another one, checked across the whole vault and, for a link that names a repository, the vault of that repository",
  "description": "A link is the one thing on a board that names something outside it, so no single board can check it: a node with nothing but its link, a board the vault does not hold, and a kind that disagrees with the level it opens (ADR 0029). A link that names a repository identity (ADR 0049) asks the same of the vault of that identity's chosen checkout, reading the target board there without migrating it, and adds two questions: whether this machine has a checkout of the repository at all, and whether the board there can be read. A link that names the vault's own repository stays in the vault, as the board listing reads it.",
  "groups": [
    "checks"
  ],
